    "body": "<!-- pr-reviewer: 79316a5dc49ff4e1592e05eac74d3b77bd7e37cc -->\n**Delta review of the hand-resolved merge of `main`. Ready for the maintainer to merge.**\n\nThis review covers only the hand resolution of the merge (b1c287a0a -> 79316a5dc). The review of `b1c287a0a` stands. The head has one new commit: the merge of `main`.\n\n### The hand resolution, hunk by hunk\nThe `git show --remerge-diff` is not empty. It has six hunks in three files. Each hunk keeps both sides. Nothing was dropped.\n\n1. `crates/app/src/operation/wire_op.rs`, imports: main's skim items (`check_passes`, `wire_passes`, `WirePass`) and the PR's `WireCorner` are both in the list.\n2. `wire_op.rs`, `condition_of`: main's `skims` field is kept in the `WireCondition` build. The PR's `taper_angle` read is added on top. Both sides are present.\n3. `wire_op.rs`, `one_condition`: main's new tuple return is kept. The burnout `clearance_door` check still runs in `condition_of` (wire_op.rs:96). `condition_of` still reads `taper_angle` (wire_op.rs:92). No check was lost in the swap.\n4. `wire_op.rs`, `generate_wire`: main's `skims_refusal` runs first, then the PR's `corner_rule` door (wire_op.rs:355-358). Both refusals are active. The 4-axis angle-word refusal is intact (wire_op.rs:434).\n5. `crates/app/src/posting_wire.rs`: both functions are present and complete. The PR's `angle_lean` keeps its three guards (posting_wire.rs:256-263): the 4-axis refusal, the `complete()` refusal, and the unresolved-top refusal. Main's `announce_skims` is kept and called (posting_wire.rs:179).\n6. `crates/app/tests/wire_taper_angle.rs`: one added line, `skims: Vec::new()`, for main's new struct field. This is a mechanical fix-up. No assertion changed.\n\nThe stamp of `taper_angle` (the safety item of the review of `9673a77e`) is intact at this head: `wire_op.rs:223-226` writes the dialect marker and both rule words. No `unwrap()`, `expect()`, or `panic!` is in the hand-edited hunks outside tests.\n\n### Gate results\nThe gate ran on the self-hosted macOS runner: https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/actions/runs/43656682722 (head merged with main `4141eb1cb` at checkout).\n\n| Step | Result |\n|---|---|\n| post suites | ok, 32 s - all binaries pass, incl. `script_wire_iso` |\n| motion suites | ok, 33 s |\n| app suites | 431 binaries ok, 1 failed: `winding_align::the_inside_out_stl_fixture_reads_inside_out_and_refuses` |\n| clippy (post, motion, app) | clean |\n\nAll wire and taper suites pass on the merged tree: `wire_taper_angle` (incl. the stamp test), `wire_taper`, `wire_4axis`, `wire_post`, `wire_contour`, `wire_stamp`, `wire_verify`, `wire_burnout`, `wire_tabs`, `posting`, `edm_machine`, `edm_conditions`, `golden_cl`, `conformance`, `project_roundtrip`, `recorded_post_streams`, `mcp_wire_contour`. U/V goldens unchanged. The head has no per-OS pinned readings, so no local arm was owed.\n\n### The one failure is not caused by this PR\n`winding_align` is unrelated to the wire files. The failure text is `left: [Outward], right: [InsideOut]`. The built tree had main's import turn (PR #1686, on main since 22:46Z) with the stale test, because the fix for that test landed on main only later, through PR #1761 (00:58Z). Main was red in that window; the runner fetched main inside it. The test on current `main` pins the turn and matches the behaviour. A merge of this branch into current `main` takes main's test file unchanged. Post-merge `main` runs verify that merge.\n\nI used this run's result per the maintainer's standing word that pr-test reports may be used. No further local build was needed: every suite in the PR's scope is green above, and the delta is the merge resolution only.\n\n### Requested before merge\nNone.\n\n### Questions / notes (not blocking)\n- The earlier `style(edm):` subject note stays as it was: harmless in the branch history.\n- The `merge-ready` label states: resolution sound, PR-scope gate green, `MERGEABLE`.\n\nA maintainer will approve and merge by hand.\n",
